@page
@model SettingsModel
@{ViewData["Title"]="Settings";}
<div class="page-title"><div class="eyebrow">// APPLICATION</div><h1>Settings</h1><p>Production configuration is supplied through environment variables or user secrets.</p></div><section class="stats"><article><small>DATABASE</small><strong>@Model.DatabaseProvider</strong><span>active provider</span></article><article><small>SMTP</small><strong>@(Model.SmtpEnabled?"ENABLED":"OFF")</strong><span>alert transport</span></article><article><small>RETENTION</small><strong>30 DAYS</strong><span>automatic cleanup</span></article><article><small>SECURITY</small><strong>COOKIE</strong><span>12-hour session</span></article></section><section class="form-panel"><h2>Database backup</h2><p>Download a snapshot of the SQLite database before upgrades or configuration changes.</p><a class="button" asp-page-handler="DownloadBackup">DOWNLOAD BACKUP</a></section><section class="form-panel"><h2>Secure configuration</h2><p>Use <code>Admin__PasswordSha256</code>, <code>Alerts__Smtp__Password</code> and connection-string environment variables in production. Never put live passwords in source control.</p></section>
